    {
      "id": "df1cda19a4a7da766582210ab049352b1291f177",
      "individual_note": true,
      "resolvable": false,
      "notes": [
        {
          "id": 465599966,
          "type": null,
          "body": "Thanks for the cleanups (uninstall and this) after my updates.\nInterestingly, the updated snappy did not break linking Wireshark on my system, so it might be interesting to investigate a bit further.\nmacos: Catalina, 10.15.7\nxcode: 11.5\nI did have linking problems linking Wireshark at first as well but I attributed that to just using cmake without the standard parameters used everywhere else and they went away after fixing that.",
          "author": {
            "id": 7354663,
            "username": "jmayer2",
            "public_email": "",
            "name": "Jörg Mayer",
            "state": "active",
            "locked": false,
            "avatar_url": "https://secure.gravatar.com/avatar/169640aaef0383905a7367726222ac4b97063ae8ad4d0f72aa58ebfe89c33a5d?s=80&d=identicon",
            "web_url": "https://gitlab.com/jmayer2"
          },
          "created_at": "2020-12-13T08:30:56.731Z",
          "updated_at": "2020-12-13T08:30:56.731Z",
          "system": false,
          "noteable_id": 81524194,
          "noteable_type": "MergeRequest",
          "project_id": 7898047,
          "resolvable": false,
          "confidential": false,
          "internal": false,
          "imported": false,
          "imported_from": "none",
          "noteable_iid": 1249,
          "commands_changes": {}
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "aafa11fa8114254e221eeceafbbc62afa1c36577",
      "individual_note": true,
      "resolvable": false,
      "notes": [
        {
          "id": 465602387,
          "type": null,
          "body": "> Interestingly, the updated snappy did not break linking Wireshark on my system\n\nI.e., the build process was linking libwireshark with a *static* libsnappy (libsnappy.a), and it didn't fail, when doing so, complaining about not finding a bunch of standard C++ library methods/routines?\n\n> macos: Catalina, 10.15.7 xcode: 11.5\n\n```\n$ sw_vers\nProductName:\tMac OS X\nProductVersion:\t10.15.7\nBuildVersion:\t19H2\n$ xcodebuild -version\nXcode 12.2\nBuild version 12B45b\n```\n\nIt failed before the update to 12.2 as well - I don't remember what it was running then, but it might have been an earlier 12.x release.",
          "author": {
            "id": 5636682,
            "username": "guyharris",
            "public_email": "",
            "name": "Guy Harris",
            "state": "active",
            "locked": false,
            "avatar_url": "https://secure.gravatar.com/avatar/1b7c243a9b1d6587a9a9067e5d83aba1e87212df7c4eeae3690f791ecbe4675a?s=80&d=identicon",
            "web_url": "https://gitlab.com/guyharris"
          },
          "created_at": "2020-12-13T08:48:52.362Z",
          "updated_at": "2020-12-13T08:48:52.362Z",
          "system": false,
          "noteable_id": 81524194,
          "noteable_type": "MergeRequest",
          "project_id": 7898047,
          "resolvable": false,
          "confidential": false,
          "internal": false,
          "imported": false,
          "imported_from": "none",
          "noteable_iid": 1249,
          "commands_changes": {}
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "72cc5125940f003f19fe987e00636d0d5fcf6815",
      "individual_note": true,
      "resolvable": false,
      "notes": [
        {
          "id": 465846111,
          "type": null,
          "body": "Looks like I had a mix of 1.1.6 and 1.1.8 installed, both static and dynamic but otool showed no dynamically linked libsnappy and tshark --version showed that it was linked against snappy but not the version.\n\nSo I deleted the libsnappy* and the snappy stuff from macos-support-libs, removed the flag for dynamic lib from macos-setup.sh, reran macos-setup.sh  and completely rebuilt Wireshark and this time I encountered the linking error as well.\n\nSo it looks like I had a mix of old and new libraries and in some strange way that was what made it work for me.\n\nSorry for the noise.",
          "author": {
            "id": 7354663,
            "username": "jmayer2",
            "public_email": "",
            "name": "Jörg Mayer",
            "state": "active",
            "locked": false,
            "avatar_url": "https://secure.gravatar.com/avatar/169640aaef0383905a7367726222ac4b97063ae8ad4d0f72aa58ebfe89c33a5d?s=80&d=identicon",
            "web_url": "https://gitlab.com/jmayer2"
          },
          "created_at": "2020-12-14T07:45:34.519Z",
          "updated_at": "2020-12-14T07:45:34.519Z",
          "system": false,
          "noteable_id": 81524194,
          "noteable_type": "MergeRequest",
          "project_id": 7898047,
          "resolvable": false,
          "confidential": false,
          "internal": false,
          "imported": false,
          "imported_from": "none",
          "noteable_iid": 1249,
          "commands_changes": {}
        }
      ]
    }
